<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;max-width:760px"><p class="kb-eye">You asked</p><h2 class="kb-h2"><span>Every brand asks us the same three questions.</span><span class="kb-i" style="color:var(--ink)">Here are the honest answers.</span></h2></div>
<div class="kb-grid kb-g3"><div class="kb-qcard"><p class="kb-q">“How do we launch in the U.S.?”</p><p class="kb-body">In front of shoppers, on day one. We put your product on a shelf or in a pop-up, bring creators to it, and tell you what sold and why. Dallas: 3,000 visitors in three days.</p></div><div class="kb-qcard"><p class="kb-q">“Who can run our pop-up in LA or New York?”</p><p class="kb-body">We do, start to finish: concept, venue, build, tickets, guest list, content. Thirty events so far in LA, Atlanta and Dallas. New York opens Dec 7.</p></div><div class="kb-qcard"><p class="kb-q">“Which agency does online and offline?”</p><p class="kb-body">Ours. The team that plans the pop-up also shoots, edits and posts it. The event feeds the content, the content fills the next event, and you get one report.</p></div></div>
</div></section>

